#**
The default rendering for a static page, used when the weblog's theme does
not supply a template named _page. Kept close to the themes' own permalink
markup so a page does not look foreign inside any of them.
*#
<!DOCTYPE html>
## lang must be a BCP-47 tag; $model.weblog.locale is Java's stored form
## ("en_US"), which no user agent recognises -- so this used to declare a
## language and effectively have none. WeblogWrapper#getLanguageTag does the
## conversion, and needs no escaping: Locale#toLanguageTag emits "und" for
## anything ill-formed rather than passing it through.
<html lang="$model.weblog.getLanguageTag()">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src * data:; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'">
    ## $model.weblog.name is pre-escaped by WeblogWrapper#getName
    ## (StringEscapeUtils.escapeHtml4) -- emit it bare, or it double-encodes
    ## ("&amp;" -> "&amp;amp;"), same as every bundled theme does. The page
    ## title is the opposite: PageBean.copyTo stores it raw, so #showPageTitle
    ## escapes it.
    <title>#showPageTitle($model.page) : $model.weblog.name</title>
    <link href="$url.absoluteSite/favicon.svg" rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" />
    #showAutodiscoveryLinks($model.weblog)
    #showSeoHead()
    #showAnalyticsTrackingCode($model.weblog)
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="$model.weblog.stylesheet">
    #showGalleryGridStyles()
    ## These five belong in the head, beside the grid styles, exactly as every
    ## bundled theme calls them: #showEmbedAssets and #showAudienceAssets bind
    ## on DOMContentLoaded, and #showGalleryAssets/#showMapAssets ship
    ## stylesheets whose late arrival at the end of <body> is a flash of
    ## unstyled gallery/map. The content assets (callouts, code blocks, heading
    ## anchors) style and enhance the article below, which carries their
    ## roller-content class for that reason.
    #showGalleryAssets()
    #showMapAssets()
    #showContentAssets()
    #showEmbedAssets()
    #showAudienceAssets()
</head>
<body>
<header>
    <p><a href="$url.home">$model.weblog.name</a></p>
    ## the page-links macro emits bare list items, so the list is ours
    <nav><ul class="page-nav">#showPageLinks($model.weblog)</ul></nav>
</header>
<main>
    <article class="roller-content">
        <h1>$utils.escapeHTML($model.page.title)</h1>
        $model.page.renderedContent
    </article>
</main>
</body>
</html>
